# TAAM Works

## Design sources

- Visual authority: [TaamWorks Figma](https://www.figma.com/design/5bLFt80FrBMHNTd7s1Zu6B/TaamWorks?node-id=0-1&p=f&m=dev). Expect ongoing layout, type, and asset edits from Dev Mode.
- Architecture / staging: `docs/taamworks-build-brief.md` (v0.2).
- Keep palette, type, spacing, and hero coordinates in CSS variables / typed config so Figma refinements do not require page rewrites.

## Brand and copy

- Preserve supplied layouts and original branding. Do not present TEMPORARY placeholders as final.
- English interface, navigation, forms, metadata, and editorial body copy only.
- Preserve Arabic (or other) lettering inside supplied artwork; do not invent bilingual UI.
- Do not fabricate project outcomes or copy inaccessible sources.

## Structure

- Homepage animation and studio/service copy are code-managed (`src/content/`).
- Portfolio content is data-driven (fixtures now; Supabase later) via a stable `Project` type.
- About and Services are homepage anchors (`/#about`, `/#services`), not separate pages.
- The three hero compositions are animation states of **one** hero (A → B → C), not three sections.
- Initiatives has no confirmed destination — do not invent a link target.
- Keep public and admin data access separate. Never expose secrets or draft/private content.
